        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "20ecc5be-7ce5-5943-8440-af2ec8f71d37",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mary Jane Phillips-Matz, Giuseppe Verdi, Antonio Ghislanzoni, Auguste Mariette, Temistocle Solera\n- Organizations: Columbia University, Smith College\n- Places: Lebanon, Ohio, Italy, United States, Busseto, Upper Manhattan, New York City\n- Works: Aida\n- Topics: Verdi research, opera source attribution, higher education\n\nFacts:\n- Columbia University was established in 1754 and is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz was born in Lebanon, Ohio and was educated at Smith College and Columbia University.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz lived for many years in Italy.\n- After returning to the United States in the early 1970s, Mary Jane Phillips-Matz spent her summers in Busseto, Giuseppe Verdi's hometown, where she continued extensive research into his life.\n- In relation to Aida, Antonio Ghislanzoni's scheme follows a scenario often attributed to Auguste Mariette.\n- Mary Jane Phillips-Matz argued that the actual source for the Aida scenario was Temistocle Solera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
